 "row_count": 21,
 "notes": [
  "GENERAL NOTE: These toughness test requirements are in addition to tests required by the material specification.",
  "(1) Carbon steels conforming to the following are subject to the limitations in Box B-2: plates in accordance with ASTM A36, A283, and A570; pipe in accordance with ASTM A134 when made from these plates; structural shapes in accordance with ASTM A992; and pipe in accordance with ASTM A53 Type F and API 5L Gr. A25 CW.",
  "(2) Impact tests that meet the requirements of Table 323.3.1-1, which are performed as part of the weld procedure qualification, will satisfy all requirements of para. 323.2.2, and need not be repeated for production welds.",
  "(3) See paras. 323.2.2(g) through 323.2.2(i).",
  "(4) Impact tests are not required when the maximum obtainable Charpy specimen has a width along the notch of less than 2.5 mm (0.098 in.). Under these conditions, and where the stress ratio defined in para. 323.2.2(b) is greater than 0.3, the design minimum temperature shall not be colder than the lower of −48°C (−55°F) or the minimum temperature for the material in Table A-1 (Table A-1C). See also para. 323.2.2(g).",
  "(5) Impact tests are not required when the maximum obtainable Charpy specimen has a width along the notch of less than 2.5 mm (0.098 in.)."
 ],
